WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.097
This is the final completion page for Module 4.

00:00:03.097 --> 00:00:07.617
The page tracks ten knowledge checks and six coding exercises.

00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:10.937
Review the counters before selecting Complete Module.

00:00:10.937 --> 00:00:17.462
If something is incomplete, the page lists the missing activity and lets you return to the relevant slide.

00:00:17.462 --> 00:00:24.762
When you select Complete Module, the browser creates an Assignment 4 submission summary containing your

00:00:24.762 --> 00:00:29.337
completion status, knowledge-check answers, and the SQL saved for each coding exercise.

00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:32.862
Review that report before copying it to Canvas.

00:00:32.862 --> 00:00:38.567
If the module is incomplete, you will be asked to confirm before copying the current progress.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:44.697
Your progress is stored locally in this browser, so changing devices, using a private window,

00:00:44.697 --> 00:00:48.167
or clearing browser storage may remove the saved state.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:52.832
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:52.832 --> 00:00:59.197
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:59.197 --> 00:01:01.507
and the shape of the expected output.

00:01:01.507 --> 00:01:07.037
In a real setting such as a retail report comparing revenue across products and regions,

00:01:07.037 --> 00:01:14.652
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:01:14.652 --> 00:01:15.037
before discussing syntax.

00:01:15.037 --> 00:01:21.561
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
